an investigation is underway this  morning after at least 27 migrants died  when their small boat capsized in the  english channel it happened yesterday  off the coast of france as mts taeb  shows us the group was traveling from  france to the uk which is a very  dangerous journey of just 21 miles  only the most desperate would be willing  to make this journey as french police  look on men women and children boarding  inflatable dinghies to cross the english  channel  before the bitterness of winter sets in  [Music]  27 people lost their lives making such  an attempt including five women and a  little girl  french lifeboat rescuer charles deval  said  there were bodies floating in the water  it was very shocking to see we recovered  six people  all dead  it was the single biggest loss of  migrant life in what is one of the  world's busiest shipping lanes since  records began in 2014. politicians on  both sides of the channel say people  smugglers are to blame  now is the time for us all to step up to  work together to do everything we can to  break these gangs who are literally  getting away with murder  but migrant rights groups say it's the  french and british governments who  helped create this crisis france for the  brutal conditions in its migrant camps  and britain for the lack of legal routes  for asylum to the uk  pushing the most vulnerable into risking  it all  now five suspected traffickers were  arrested overnight but until britain and  france can come up with meaningful  solutions to this crisis  more will likely lose their lives dana  mts tayab in london thank you
 

